  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#the-canvas-element:offscreencanvas-2\r\n\r\n>  and the content of the canvas element is updated by calling the `commit\\(\\)` method of the OffscreenCanvas object's rendering context\\.\r\n\r\nThere's no `commit` method and no plans to add one.\r\n\r\nReferences to `commit` should be removed from the spec.\r\n\r\nAn `OffscreenCanvas` created via `transferControlToOffscreen` and rendered to from a worker work the same as the main page. When the worker exits an event in which it has called something in the a context that would cause changes to the content of a canvas the browser automatically queues the appropriate things to happen so the results show up on the page.\r\n\r\nKen, Kelsey, if you have better references that this part of the spec is out of date please add them. \r\n\r\n@kenrussell @kdashg ",
